# Template for ~/.leadgen/.env — the one config file this skill reads.
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.leadgen && cp .env.example ~/.leadgen/.env
#
# It lives in your home directory, not in a project and not inside the installed skill,
# so the same keys work from every folder, on every agent, and survive a reinstall.
#
# WHY EVERY NAME STARTS WITH LEADGEN_
# Nothing here can collide with another CLI. A key stored under a shared name like
# OPENAI_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY silently switches Claude Code and Codex from the
# subscription you already pay for to API billing. This project owns its own namespace and
# never reads a variable another tool might also read.

# --- Scraping (required) ---
LEADGEN_FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...   # site URL mapping, stage 1 only (firecrawl.com)
LEADGEN_ZYTE_API_KEY=...           # every page fetch, stages 2-4 (zyte.com)

# --- LLM (required) ---
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Two roles; point both at one model if you prefer.
#   reasoning  = ranks pages, judges ambiguous email formats
#   extraction = pulls {name, title, email} out of page text
LEADGEN_LLM_API_KEY=...
LEADGEN_LLM_BASE_URL=              # leave empty for api.openai.com
LEADGEN_LLM_MODEL_REASONING=gpt-4o
LEADGEN_LLM_MODEL_EXTRACTION=gpt-4o-mini

# Base URLs, if you are not using OpenAI directly:
#   OpenRouter  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   Together    https://api.together.xyz/v1
#   Groq        https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   Ollama      http://localhost:11434/v1        (LEADGEN_LLM_API_KEY=ollama)
#   Azure       https://<resource>.cognitiveservices.azure.com/openai/v1/
#               and use your DEPLOYMENT NAMES as the two model names above.

# --- Open-web discovery (OPTIONAL — stage 5 is skippable) ---
# Codex is NOT required. Without it, stage 5 is skipped and the rest runs normally.
# Codex uses the ChatGPT login (run `codex login`), NOT an API key here.
# IMPORTANT: keep OPENAI_API_KEY UNSET, here and in your shell. The runner unsets it for
# the Codex child process so Codex uses your subscription instead of billing a key.
LEADGEN_CODEX_BIN=codex            # optional; resolved from PATH by default
LEADGEN_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol    # optional

# --- Optional ---
# LEADGEN_OUT_DIR=/path/to/out     # results go to ./out in the current folder by default
# LEADGEN_DEBUG=1                  # verbose agent step tracing on stderr
